      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Located on Puerto Rico’s southern coast, Salinas borders the Caribbean Sea and is known for its beautiful beaches and the birthplace of mojo isleño.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.exploreholyoke.com/salinas-puerto-rico/",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town hosts the Albergue Olímpico, a sports complex that once served as an Olympic hostel and remains a hub for local athletes.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salinas%2C_Puerto_Rico",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Salinas claims a role in the invention of volleyball, a fact celebrated by its sister city Holyoke and highlighted in local lore.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
